   "id": 613659,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Two hikers take different routes to reach the same spot. The first one goes <span data-math=\"255\\,\\text{m}\">255\\,\\text{m}</span> southeast, then turns and goes <span data-math=\"82\\,\\text{m}\">82\\,\\text{m}</span> at <span data-math=\"14^\\circ\\!\">14^\\circ\\!</span> south of east. The second hiker goes <span data-math=\"200\\,\\text{m}\">200\\,\\text{m}</span> south. How far and in which direction must the second hiker travel now, in order to reach the first hiker's location destination?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1162663,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"200\\,\\text{m}\">200\\,\\text{m}</span> east"
    },
    {
